VENUE HIGHLIGHTS



BOSTON:

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 7
Stadium Facts: Built in 1970. Capacity 61,000.
Distance: Foxboro Stadium is located halfway between Boston, MA and Providence, RI, approximately 20 miles from downtown Boston.
June/July weather: average temperature is 70.5 degrees F/21 degrees C.

Attractions: Boston dates back to the American Revolution and is a fabled cradle of American liberty. Boston grew as a harbor town and is still one of the nation's finest ports. The city is now a center of banking and finance. Tourists can visit Boston Common, Faneuil Hall, the Swan Boats, and the U.S.S. Constitution. More than 20 colleges and universities are located in Boston, including Harvard University, the oldest college in the United States.












CHICAGO:

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 3
Stadium Facts: Built in 1922. Capacity 66,946.
Distance: Soldier Field is ideally located on the shore of Lake Michigan, south of downtown Chicago, Illinois.
June/July Weather: average temperature is 70 degrees F/21.1 degrees C.

Attractions: Housing major air, rail and highway hubs, Chicago has historically remained a vibrant pulse of transportation. Tourists can visit the Museum of Science and Industry, the Field Museum of Natural History, the Chicago Art Institute, and the Lincoln Park Zoo. Three of the five tallest man-made structures in the world give Chicago a world-famous skyline. Chicago will host the Opening Ceremonies and Opening Match of the 1994 World Cup.






DALLAS:

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 9
Stadium Facts: Built in 1930, located in historic Fair Park, home of the annual state fair of Texas. Capacity 67,600.
Distance: The Cotton Bowl is located in downtown Dallas.
June/July weather: average temperature is 83 degrees F/28.3 degrees C.

Attractions: Located in the heart of northern Texas, Dallas boasts a broad economic base. Known for its production of oil and natural gas, Dallas also houses one of the largest inland cotton markets, thus the name Cotton Bowl. Tourist can visit the Dallas Garden Center, the Dallas Historical Society Museum, and the Dallas Symphony Orchestra. Dallas will be the site of the 1994 World Cup International Broadcast Center.

















DETROIT

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 6
Stadium Facts: Built in 1975, this domed indoor stadium will have natural grass put in place for the 1994 World Cup. Capacity 80,435.
Distance: The Silverdome is in Pontiac, Michigan, 18 miles from downtown Detroit.
June/July weather: average temperature is 71 degrees F/21.7 degrees C. 
Temperature inside dome: average temperature is 70 degrees F/21 degrees C.

Attractions: The automotive industry made its home in metropolitan Detroit in the 1920's and Detroit became synonymous with the car and American manufacturing skill. In the 1960's, Detroit gave rise to the Motown recording label and stars such as the Jackson 5, Stevie Wonder, and the Supremes. Today, the 1,000 acre Belle Isle Park attracts tourists with its beautiful beaches, yacht basin, zoo,aquarium and botanical garden.




















LOS ANGELES:

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 2
Stadium Facts: Built in 1922, famous for the Rose Bowl game held annually on New Year's Day. Capacity 102,083.
Distance: The Rose Bowl in Pasadena, CA is seven miles from downtown Los Angeles.
June/July weather: average temperature is 71degrees F/21.7 degrees C.

Attractions: By 1910, Los Angeles was already well known as the motion picture capital of the world. The city has 46 miles of waterfront a superb highway system. Los Angeles was the home of the 1932 and 1984 Olympic Games. The charming town of Pasadena is famous for the annual Tournament of Roses Parade and the Rose Bowl game. The Rose Bowl will be the site of the 1994 World Cup Final Match.













NEW YORK/NEW JERSEY

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 1
Stadium Facts: Built in 1976, home of the New York Cosmos soccer team 1977-1984. Capacity 76,891.
Distance: Giants Stadium is part of the Meadowlands Complex located in East Rutherford, New Jersey, approximately five miles from New York City.
June/July weather: average temperature is 74 degrees F/23.3 degrees C. 

Attractions: New Jersey boasts attractions such as Atlantic City and Princeton University. Known as the Garden State, New Jersey is famous for its extensive small scale agriculture. New York City is just across the Hudson River from Giants Stadium, approximately a five mile drive. Tourists can visit the Empire State Building, Statue of Liberty, United Nations, Times Square, Central Park, or go shopping and enjoy all there is to do in New York City!


















ORLANDO 

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 37
Stadium Facts: Built in 1976, home of the annual Florida Citrus Bowl. Capacity 70,188.
Distance: The Citrus Bowl is located one mile west of downtown Orlando.
June/July weather: average temperature is 81 degrees F/27.2 degrees C. 

Attractions: Orlando is the center of one of the U.S.' fastest growing areas. Famous for the world's most popular tourist attraction, Walt Disney World Magic Kingdom, millions of visitors flock to central Florida every year. Epcot Center, Disney MGM Studios, Sea World, Universal Studios Florida and Kennedy Space Center are also in the area. Orlando has nearly 100 golf courses, tennis courts and many water sports to enjoy in the Florida sunshine.


























WASHINGTON, D.C.

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 8
Stadium Facts: Built in 1961. Capacity 56,500.
Distance: Robert F. Kennedy Memorial Stadium is located 20 blocks east of the U.S. Capitol Building in downtown Washington, D.C.
June/July weather: average temperature is 77 degrees F/25 degrees C. 

Attractions: The capital of the United States, Washington, D.C. is filled with history and tradition. The monuments and museums are plentiful. Tourists can visit the White House, the U.S. Capitol, the Washington Monument, the Library of Congress, the Smithsonian Institution Museums, and the National Zoo. The Smithsonian Air and Space Museum is one of the busiest museums in the world. Washington, D.C. is conveniently located near beaches and mountains.











SAN FRANCISCO

Population: Metropolitan area USA Rank: 4
Stadium Facts: Built in 1921, the stadium of Stanford University. Capacity 86,019.
Distance: Stanford Stadium is in Palo Alto, CA and is located 27 miles south of downtown San Francisco.
June/July weather: average temperature is 59 degrees F/15 degrees C. 

Attractions: San Francisco survived a devastating earthquake in 1906 and thrives today as a major cosmopolitan city and a prominent transportation and industrial center. More than 40 steamship lines use San Francisco as a port of call, importing merchandise from all over the world. Tourists can visit Fisherman's Wharf, Chinatown and ride historic cable cars. Palo Alto is a residential community with many parks, libraries and community centers.

